{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l22wa08s","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"physics","chapter":"electromagnetic-induction","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"magnetic-flux-faradays-and-lenzs-laws","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"pa-current-carrying-infinitely-long-wire-is-kept-along-the-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-9xn5p2ywj3dmfu0g","content":"<p>A current carrying infinitely long wire is kept along the diameter of a circular wire loop, without touching it, the correct statement(s) is(are)</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"the emf induced in the loop is zero if the current is constant."},{"identifier":"B","content":"the emf induced in the loop is finite if the current is constant."},{"identifier":"C","content":"the emf induced in the loop is zero if the current decreases at a steady state"},{"identifier":"D","content":"the emf induced in the loop is finite if the current decreases at a steady state."}],"correct_options":["A","C"],"explanation":"<p>The magnetic field due to an infinitely long conductor is circumferential.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l26hlply/5e0ba735-e0aa-4159-9c3c-8ea9774ce8b3/97952860-c00f-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hlplz.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l26hlply/5e0ba735-e0aa-4159-9c3c-8ea9774ce8b3/97952860-c00f-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hlplz.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Electromagnetic Induction Question 15 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l26hlply/5e0ba735-e0aa-4159-9c3c-8ea9774ce8b3/97952860-c00f-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hlplz.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l26hlply/5e0ba735-e0aa-4159-9c3c-8ea9774ce8b3/97952860-c00f-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hlplz.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l26hlply/5e0ba735-e0aa-4159-9c3c-8ea9774ce8b3/97952860-c00f-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hlplz.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l26hlply/5e0ba735-e0aa-4159-9c3c-8ea9774ce8b3/97952860-c00f-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hlplz.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l26hlply/5e0ba735-e0aa-4159-9c3c-8ea9774ce8b3/97952860-c00f-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hlplz.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l26hlply/5e0ba735-e0aa-4159-9c3c-8ea9774ce8b3/97952860-c00f-11ec-8e78-8beb702b8cb9/file-1l26hlplz.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Since this conductor is placed along the diameter of circular loop (see figure), the total magnetic flux through the circular wire loop is always zero.</p>"}]}